# MERIT.instructions (SPRK student-safe)

This file is the public, student-safe adaptation of enterprise MERIT AgenticOps for `SPRK-Hello-Repo`. It does not copy private vault text, operator secrets, or machine-specific paths from the enterprise MERIT instruction set.

## Purpose

- Give students and coding agents one canonical rules file for how this repository is organized.
- Keep classroom missions consistent, testable, and easy to navigate.

## Mission folder naming (required)

Every playable mission under `missions/` must use exactly one folder with this shape:

```text
NN-GameName-<mode-label>
```

| Part | Rule | Example |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `NN` | Two-digit mission number; matches menu, docs, and Playwright registry | `10` |
| `GameName` | PascalCase mission name; no spaces; no internal hyphens | `SpaceInvaders`, `SnakeGame` |
| `<mode-label>` | Player/sync mode: `1P`, `2P`, `nP`, `1P-nP`, or `2P-nP` | `1P-nP` |

Valid examples already in this repo:

- `01-ReactionRace-nP`
- `02-SnakeGame-1P-nP`
- `03-PingPong-2P-nP`
- `10-SpaceInvaders-1P-nP`

Invalid patterns (do not introduce):

- `10-Space-Invaders` (hyphenated game name; missing mode label)
- `missions/10-Space-Invaders` alongside `missions/10-SpaceInvaders-1P-nP` (duplicate mission folders)
- Mission app files in the repository root

Scaffold for the next mission: copy `missions/XX-Template-nP/` and rename to the real `NN-GameName-<mode-label>` before adding gameplay.

When adding a mission, also register it in `tests/helpers/start-mission-server.js`, `tests/helpers/run-playwright.js`, and `package.json` test scripts.

## Mode labels

| Label | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `1P` | One player |
| `2P` | Two players |
| `nP` | Many players (classroom) |
| `1P-nP` | Starts single-player; can grow to classroom multiplayer |
| `2P-nP` | Starts two-player; can grow to classroom multiplayer |

The folder suffix must match the Mode column in `README.md` Mission Menu.

## Repository shape

- Root: workspace files only (`README.md`, `package.json`, `docs/`, `tests/`, instruction files).
- `missions/<NN-GameName-mode>/`: each mission’s `index.html`, `server.py`, `src/`, and `docs/`.
- `missions/_shared/`: shared backend/frontend helpers and generated baseline status.
- `tests/`: Playwright specs and artifacts (not committed when generated during local runs).

Do not rename `docs/` to a MERIT `{Name} docs/` folder in this student repo; curriculum links depend on `docs/`.

## Validation before confidence

From the repository root:

```bash
npm run setup:missions
npm run validate
```

Mission-specific quick check:

```bash
npm run test:spaceinvaders
```

A mission change is not ready until the relevant Playwright baseline passes and only intended files are staged.

## Student-safe MERIT principles

1. Single source of truth — link to an existing guide instead of duplicating long explanations.
2. Validation before confidence — Playwright baseline and Baseline Status tab reflect real backends.
3. Secrets stay local — use `.env.local` if needed; commit only `.env.example` templates.
4. No hard-coded machine paths — use repo-relative paths and helpers.
5. Recovery over mystery — errors and docs should say what to try next.

